    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** headlining the offense, boasting a team-high 81.88 efficiency score. **Gunnar Henderson** draws a favorable matchup against May, benefiting from a potent +16% park adjustment and an aggressive +14% dynamic platoon edge. Alongside him, **Jackson Merrill** (72.12) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.43) provide excellent production stability. **Heliot Ramos** (66.10) is a high-upside play today, bolstered by an additional +2% boost due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which creates a prime opportunity for him to exploit the stolen base scarcity that remains our top priority. **Miguel Vargas** (65.14) also presents a strong play, as his high xwOBA (0.379) and leadoff status maximize his value against a pedestrian Sears, A.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Josh Jung**, who landed at a 41.45 efficiency score. While **Josh Jung** is a capable hitter, his matchup against Cease\u2014a high-end arm with a 3.06 xERA\u2014resulted in a -19% SP skill penalty, pushing him below the threshold required to displace our starters. Elsewhere, **Wade Meckler** failed to clear our 40-point \"Zebras Floor\" due to a disadvantageous left-on-left platoon matchup and a bottom-of-the-order assignment, forcing him to the bench. While the lineup is set, we must remain vigilant regarding the health of **Jordan Westburg** and **Luis Robert Jr.**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL, further thinning our depth as we navigate the final stretch of the season.",
